--TEST--
An `[app.settings]` value replaces the `[settings]` value of the same name for that application, an `[app.secrets]` value replaces the `[secrets]` one, and a key the block does not write keeps the global value — `rule:config/settings-and-secrets-are-a-programs-own-values`
--FILE nvs.toml--
[settings]
title = "Store"
page_size = 10

[secrets]
api_key = "global-key"

[[app]]
root = "."

[app.settings]
page_size = 50

[app.secrets]
api_key = "shop-key"
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The application block sets `page_size`, so its value is used.
echo Core\Config::setting('page_size') as int, "\n";
// The application block does not set `title`, so the global value is used.
echo Core\Config::setting('title') as string, "\n";
// The application secret is used. The program cannot print a secret, so it prints the comparison.
echo Core\Config::secret('api_key') == 'shop-key' ? "shop" : "global", "\n";
--EXPECT--
50
Store
shop
